From: AX6 offline repair review
Subject: [PATCH 009] nss-dp: isolate IPQ807x on overlay detach

Base: qca-nss-dp d8f802f08fd8ff31057ba58edb20bbe448e7b505,
fully prepared with exact current 001-008 from source
2e207fcae4479bc55211fb83395ae2954b39b951.

Use an IPQ807x per-port callback/context reader gate and RTNL-owned
writers. Block and drain existing readers before installing DP-owned
permanent quarantine. Never select or reinitialize EDMA on detach;
never send NSS close/deinit commands on the detached path. Preserve
other-SoC valid-input dispatch behavior.

No hardware ring/IRQ or firmware configuration is changed. This patch
is a source-only containment candidate, not hot recovery or a deployment.
NSS RX registry/netdev lifetime must be drained independently by the
registry owner before freeing netdev. Generic DP/NSS hot-unbind remains
outside this candidate's proof.

